      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Specs for kernel capabilities that are proposed but not built. This tier is non-normative: a spec records the motivating problem, a proposed shape, the alternatives weighed, and what is still open. It never describes current behavior. When a feature ships, its contracts move into "
        },
        {
          "insert": "10-system-design/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "20-implementation/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the spec shrinks to a pointer at them. Working notes that are not yet specs stay in "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".drafts/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
